# tests/cooker/determinism.sha256 -- THE FROZEN COOK-DETERMINISM MANIFEST (task 3.3.3).
#
# SHA-256 of the artifact each of twenty fixed aero_cooker invocations produces. The invocations
# live in tests/cooker/run_case.cmake's `golden_manifest` (6, mesh), `texture_golden_manifest`
# (8, texture), `skeleton_golden_manifest` (1, skeleton), `animation_golden_manifest`
# (3, animation) and `audio_golden_manifest` (2, audio) arms; those five ctest cases check every
# line of this file in every build configuration on every lane, and .github/workflows/ci.yml's
# `cook-determinism` job checks the same lines a second time with coreutils sha256sum and
# byte-compares the three lanes' copies.
#
# THIS FILE IS FROZEN. A changed line means THE SAME INPUT NOW COOKS TO DIFFERENT BYTES -- which is,
# verbatim, docs/09-file-formats.md section 9.11's definition of a cookerVersion bump. So a
# regeneration travels IN THE SAME COMMIT as the cook change and the matching
# COOKED_MESH_COOKER_VERSION / COOKED_TEXTURE_COOKER_VERSION / COOKED_SKELETON_COOKER_VERSION /
# COOKED_ANIMATION_COOKER_VERSION / COOKED_AUDIO_COOKER_VERSION bump, with the pull request saying
# why.
# NEVER EDIT A HASH TO GREEN A RED RUN.
#
# To regenerate, when and only when the change is deliberate:
#   1. cmake --build --preset <host>-release
#   2. ctest --preset <host>-release \
#        -R 'cooker\.(golden|texture_golden|skeleton_golden|animation_golden|audio_golden)_manifest'
#      THAT REGEX IS PART OF THE RITUAL: leaving an arm out of it SILENTLY SKIPS that arm's lines
#      during a regeneration, which is exactly the trap task 3.5.1 recorded when the fourth arm
#      landed. `ctest -N` with the same -R must list FIVE cases.
#   3. each failing case prints its new `<sha256>  <name>` lines verbatim, one per line; paste them
#      in, re-run, and confirm green in BOTH the debug and the release preset.
#
# TWO PAIRS OF NAMES SHARE ONE HASH ON PURPOSE, and the second pair is stronger evidence than the
# first. mesh-triangle and mesh-external cook to the same 272 bytes because external.gltf carries the
# same geometry as triangle.gltf and where a buffer came from never reaches the file. audio-tone-wav
# and audio-tone-flac cook to the same 16064 bytes because dr_wav and dr_flac -- two different
# decoders reading two different containers -- recover the same 8000 s16 frames from tone.wav and the
# flac encoded from it; that equality is the single strongest line in this file, since a backend wired
# to the wrong decoder or a transposed sample would break it and no single-decoder arm could see it.
# Lookup is by NAME; do not add a distinct-hash check.
#
# THE HALVES ARE NOT ANCHORED EQUALLY, AND THE ASYMMETRY IS REAL. There are three kinds of anchor
# in this file and it is worth knowing which one a red line is carrying.
#
# (1) mesh-triangle's line is independently derivable: it equals the SHA-256 of
# COOKED_GOLDEN_TRIANGLE's 272 bytes in tests/cooked_mesh_golden.hpp, a golden frozen by task 3.3.1
# with no cooker involved, so at least one mesh line cannot be self-confirming.
#
# (2) NO TEXTURE LINE HAS AN EQUIVALENT TIE -- the four texture byte goldens pin the cook layer on
# in-memory inputs, not this file's CLI path, so the eight texture hashes are anchored only by having
# been generated once and frozen. What keeps them honest is external: ci.yml's cook-determinism job
# runs Khronos ktx validate over every cooked .ktx2 on every push, and that is the one check our own
# code cannot self-confirm (our parser compares the descriptor against the same tables our writer
# emits). Read a red texture line with that in mind.
#
# (3) The two audio lines (task 3.7.1) carry a THIRD, different tie, and it is worth stating exactly
# rather than overclaiming. Their BULK REGION is externally anchored: tests/fixtures/audio's
# tone.s16le.pcm is ffmpeg's OWN decode of tone.wav -- raw interleaved s16 LE produced by libavcodec
# and by nothing of ours -- and aero_tests' AK17 and the editor suite's AD10/AD11 assert that our
# decode and our cook reproduce those bytes exactly. That anchors the DECODE, which is the half no
# tool of ours can self-confirm; the 64-byte header and therefore these two frozen hashes are still
# anchored only by having been generated once. Neither audio line is derivable the way
# mesh-triangle's is.
#
# The skeleton and animation lines carry no external tie of any kind.

